            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Scandinavia",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Further, the geographic pattern of these temperature changes associated with Younger Dryas is as expected if they were caused by the conveyor turning on. Pronounced changes are confined to latitudes > 40\u00b0N and extend from the maritime provinces of Canada and the ice cap of Greenland on the west across the northern Atlantic, the British Isles, and Scandinavia into Russia on the east (for summary see Rind et al., 1986).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Younger Dryas",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Russia",
            "target_entity_type": "Country",
            "paragraph": "Further, the geographic pattern of these temperature changes associated with Younger Dryas is as expected if they were caused by the conveyor turning on. Pronounced changes are confined to latitudes > 40\u00b0N and extend from the maritime provinces of Canada and the ice cap of Greenland on the west across the northern Atlantic, the British Isles, and Scandinavia into Russia on the east (for summary see Rind et al., 1986).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
